# Visual Iteration with Godot MCP

When fixing visual/rendering issues (shaders, UI, placement, particles, terrain), use the Godot MCP to verify changes instead of coding blind:

1. Make the code/shader change
2. Run the game via `editor` → `run`
3. Ask the user to navigate to the relevant area (e.g. "Walk to a river so I can screenshot it")
4. Use `editor` → `screenshot_game` to capture the result
5. Evaluate the screenshot — if the fix isn't right, iterate
6. Use `editor` → `stop` when done

Also use `editor` → `get_errors` and `get_log_messages` to catch runtime issues after changes.

Do NOT skip the visual verification loop for rendering or spatial changes. Always confirm visually before marking a task complete.
